      "message": "Van der Waerden: closed maintainer profile for OpenAI's own ProgressionColoring solution (c = 1/100000)\n\nLead task 55f01df6 (2026-11-06; verifier#150 asked for a rerun of a byte copy of OpenAI's\nsolution, which has no route). Precedents: critical-line-zeros (a closed rerun of the\nstatement owner's own proof) and matrix-nine-fourths (openai/math on our default pins, a\nsource prefix and a sparse clone).\n\nThe trusted challenge is openai/math 1581d4cb lean/ComparatorChallenges/\nQuantitativeVanDerWaerden.lean, byte for byte (blob bee3f5a8, Mathlib only). Its one theorem,\nOAI.QuantitativeVanDerWaerden.uniform_lower_bound, is the board quantity at c = 1/100000:\nexists K, forall k >= K, forall r >= 2, k^((1/100000) k Nat.log 2 r) < W r k. Solution module,\ntheorem and axioms as in their Comparator config QuantitativeVanDerWaerden.json.\n\nPins: our defaults, which are theirs at this commit (Lean v4.34.1, Mathlib d13f23b7,\nprofiles/tools.json); autoImplicit false as their lakefile. Sources: sparse checkout of\nlean/OAI/Combinatorics/ProgressionColoring/, root OAI, prefix that folder. Their other\npackages and compatibility patches are outside the import closure, so no\nsolution_dependencies. An offline plan on the real tree at 1581d4cb (nothing built) staged\n115 files (643 KB) and planned 115 modules in 48 chains; a text scan found no sorry, admit\ntactic or axiom in them.\n\nComparator #68 does not apply: its Lean fix (leanprover/lean4#14728, merged 2026-08-10) is in\nv4.34.1, and the challenge declares no structure.\n\nClosed: no direct.json entry; only a maintainer dispatch of verify.yml runs it. No verifier\ncode change. Upstream LICENSE next to the statement (openai/math has no NOTICE); NOTICE and\ndocs/targets.md entries. No Lean ran on any of our machines. Tests:\ntests/test_van_der_waerden.py (7); 290 pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
